TY  - JOUR
T1  - Commentary on Pessaret al.: ‘Downscaling’ United States state cannabis policy to investigate environmental and social impacts on cannabis use
AN  - 3175968912; 2025-59189-006
AB  - Comments on an article by Seema Choksy Pessar et al.(see record 2025-59189-005). Pessar et al. offer a key scientific advance by treating state level cannabis policy as a continuous variable that reflects the degree of legal restrictions on cannabis use, cultivation, distribution, advertising and other characteristics. This contrasts with the vast majority of cannabis policy impact studies that have used a simple, dichotomous classification of legal versus illegal. Pessar et al. approach, therefore, offers a more sensitive and precise measure of the variation in cannabis policies across the states and, consequently, a greater weight of evidence regarding the impact of liberalizing cannabis policy on the prevalence of cannabis use. Analogous to Pessar et al. innovation in the precision of measurement of cannabis policy, recent advances in geospatial technologies and methods afford fine-scale measurement of individual level environmental exposures for modeling pathways from environmental and social contextual forces to cannabis use. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
