TY  - JOUR
T1  - Digital phenotyping and mobile sensing in addiction psychiatry
AN  - 2608161550; 2022-04112-005
AB  - The letter discusses the integration of digital phenotyping and mobile sensing in addiction psychiatry. Potential advantages are discussed when addressing shortcomings within psychiatry. It is noted that psychiatry lacks reliable tests that predict illness risk, treatment response, remission, or recurrence likelihood. It is noted that the overarching challenge is to realize an integration of digital phenotyping and mobile sensing into substance use disorder diagnostic assessments, coupled to discovery of underlying mechanisms and delivery of targeted interventions. It is argued that the attractions of digital personalized medicine arises out of a deployment capability within a clinical environment, one tat addresses the challenge of salability. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
