T1  - Commentary on Sacks-Daviset al. (2016): Quantifying the risk environment—Effect modification and precision population health
AN  - 1837610542; 2016-48885-011
AB  - Comments on an article by Rachel Sacks‐Davis et al. (see record 2016-36354-001). Substance use epidemiology focuses increasingly on the risk environment; however, few studies quantify the differential impacts of physical, social and structural environments on population health risk factors and outcomes. To do so, researchers studying the effects of the risk environment on drug-related harms should consider effect modification analyses.Sacks‐Davis, Rachel (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
