T1  - Exposure exposed
AN  - 1509631567; 2013-34029-022
AB  - Comments on the articles by Thomas R. Kirchner et al. (see record 2013-34029-004) and Michael Jerrett et al. (see record 2013-34029-005). The work by Kirchner et al. describes exposure to point-of-sale tobacco materials and its relationship with lapses in smoking cessation. The paper by Jerrett and colleagues assessed neighborhood physical activity in a smart-growth community. Both papers smoothly created exposure variables, matching locations to behavioral outcomes, which is genuine progress for this field. Kirchner's analyzed employed standard ArcGIS tools to match the GPS tracks with the point-of-sale tobacco outlets. Because of the computational challenges of such analyses, many researchers are migrating to PostgreSQL geo-databases to manage the queries and employing environmental raster layers that can be represented in a binary format instead of geometric shape-based data that are represented by data strings. Data management guidelines for public health researchers attempting to conduct this work would be beneficial. Jerrett et al. mentioned processing some of their data in R, an open source system. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
