TY  - JOUR
T1  - At odds with science?
AN  - 1348795288; 2013-09839-041
AB  - Comments on an article by I. Lund & J. Scheffels (see record 2012-02460-006). Lund and Scheffels discussed survey data on Norwegian general practitioners’ (GP) perception of the harmfulness of snus, and the same GPs’ tendency not to recommend snus in smoking cessation. Their abstract concluded that "almost two thirds of GPs had beliefs about the relative risk of snus and cigarettes that were at odds with scientific consensus." The authors also expressed worry of an "unexploited intervention potential." In our view, Lund and Scheffels’ conclusion that Norwegian GPs were “at odds with scientific consensus” leading to an “unexploited intervention potential” therefore seems disputable. It may promote unwarranted doubt and distrust to GPs and to Norwegian health authorities. There is a lasting conflict of interest between national health authorities and the tobacco industry. It is therefore important to be careful with the use of references and the choice of statements in order to avoid unintended support for this industry. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
