T1  - Supporting GPS in the provision of smoking cessation intervention--From research to daily routine: Comment
AN  - 622077405; 2008-00720-021
AB  - We are grateful for the comments by Maxine Stitzer (see record 2008-00720-019) and Martin Edwards (see record 2008-00720-020) on the original article (see record 2008-00720-018) because they show that implementing effective interventions for smoking cessation in primary medical care is a challenge, even in countries that have progressed much more in the prevention of tobacco-attributable death and disease than the nation in which the data of our study have been collected. Stimulated by the comments we would like to discuss two problems that have to be solved in the near future: (i) how should we deal with the complexity and heterogeneity of general practice settings; and (ii) what are the next steps for research to optimize interventions for routine care? (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
