TY  - JOUR
T1  - Roles and responsibilities of doctors in the provision of treatment for drug and alcohol misusers
AN  - 620981026; 2005-14363-017
AB  - This document reflects the findings of a working group set up jointly by the Royal College of Psychiatrists and the Royal College of General Practitioners. There has been a large increase in the number of doctors from a range of professional backgrounds working with substance misusers. This increase has mainly been in primary care, as there are shortages of addiction psychiatrists and other experts in secondary care. General Medical Services contract has defined locally and nationally enhanced services, which allow a degree of clarity in terms of the services a GP would be expected to provide to a drug misuser. In some parts of the country, GPs are working as primary care addiction specialists. Doctors work within treatment systems and therefore may provide services over a range of National Treatment Agency Models of Care tiers. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
