T1  - Don't scold smokers
AN  - 620803533; 2005-07089-014
AB  - In response to a recent paper (see record 2004-18616-004) about GPs' difficulties with smokers who are not motivated to quit, points to consider are: (1) nicotine is one of the strongest addictions; (2) smokers hold various beliefs about smoking, and doctors should consider how to communicate risk; (3) confrontation is contraindicated; and (4) some smokers deceive doctors about their smoking. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
