TY  - JOUR
T1  - Controlling cancer pain in primary care: The prescribing habits and knowledge base of general practitioners
AN  - 619879917; 2002-13596-003
AB  - Examined the prescribing habits and knowledge of general practitioners (GPs) concerning certain key advanced cancer pain control issues. 330 GPs (aged <35-55+ yrs) completed questionnaires concerning prescription habits, treatment options, and examination styles. Results show that most Ss were familiar with the modern management of cancer pain, including the World Health Organization approach, the use of oral opioids, and the management of bone pain. Less awareness was reported concerning drug options available for more uncommon situations, especially the dose conversion of oral morphine to subcutaneous diamorphine and drugs that may be used in syringe drivers. The employed questionnaire is appended. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2018 APA, all rights reserved)
