TY  - JOUR
T1  - Combining qualitative interviews with video-recorded consultations: Gaining insight into GPs' decision-making
AN  - 619414151; 1999-05609-004
AB  - Used a combination of semi-structured interviews and video-recorded consultations to research the influences on decisions made by 42 GPs during their consultations. The authors describe the use of GPs' video-recorded consultations as a stimulus for focused, semi-structured interviews and discuss how this research method compares with other approaches for studying GPs' decision-making during consultations. GPs' surgery sessions were video-recorded and later they were shown video recordings of themselves consulting with smokers before participating in semi-structured interviews about these consultations. The interviews were aimed to describe the factors which GPs perceived to influence their decisions to discuss or not discuss smoking with patients. This technique can be used to research decisions, which are made frequently by GPs. It is probably most appropriate for gaining insight into decision-making during mundane consultations, to which GPs would otherwise give little thought. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
