TY  - JOUR
T1  - Are all districts equally ready for "shared care" of drug misusers?
AN  - 619531436; 2000-14302-003
AB  - 341 general practitioners (GPs) in 3 neighboring districts with varied sociodemographic characteristics in the UK were sent a questionnaire concerning attitudes toward drug misusers and their treatment beliefs and knowledge. 79% (270) returned completed questionnaires. Two of the districts showed similar attitude scores toward opiate users and their treatment but the 3rd district contained significantly more GPs with negative attitudes. Social deprivation scores did not appear to be important. GPs who had experience in prescribing for drug users and were younger were more likely to have positive opinions. This study demonstrates an apparent positive shift in opinion and attitude of GPs and provides indications for purchasers wishing to develop "shared care" of drug misusers. However they must first assess local conditions before they can set targets and allocate resources. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
