TY  - JOUR
T1  - Needs of special groups: Drug and alcohol problems
AN  - 619354209; 1998-10310-010
AB  - Discusses how, despite frequent contact with alcohol and drug using patients, these problems still go undetected by general practitioners (GPs) in the primary care setting. The author contends that, because the attitudes of GPs are of central importance in determining their involvement with drug and alcohol misusers, GP education must be oriented toward acceptance of the legitimacy and rewards involved in working with this population. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
