TY  - JOUR
T1  - Prevalence of alcohol problems in general practice: An experience from Southern Italy
AN  - 618867386; 1996-05879-003
AB  - The Michigan Alcoholism Screening Test (MAST) and the response to a question about heavy alcohol consumption were used to assess the prevalence of alcohol problems in 77 male and 46 female patients (aged 18–83 yrs) consulting a GP. Alcohol problems were identified in 45 males and 9 females (43.9% of total sample). The prevalence of MAST positive Ss was 32.5% in the total patient sample, 45.5% among males and 10.9% among females. The question about heavy alcohol consumption had a predictive positive value of 73.1% for identifying MAST positive Ss. It is suggested that GPs should incorporate this question about heavy alcohol consumption as a screening question to detect alcohol problems and give advice regarding reduction of alcohol consumption. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
