TY  - JOUR
T1  - Screening for cardiovascular disease and risk reduction counselling behaviors of general practitioners
AN  - 618518367; 1994-46524-001
AB  - Describes the prevalence of risk factors for cardiovascular disease in general practice patients and risk factor detection and preventive care (PC) activities of general practitioners (GPs) in Australia. In a cross-sectional study of 230 GPs and 7,160 patients, self-report data on patient risk factors and rates of screening and data on GPs' knowledge of patient risk factors and PC provided during consultation were analyzed. The results show that screening and counseling of patients was highest for blood pressure and smoking and considerably lower for the risk factors of weight, alcohol, and cholesterol. Lack of confidence, lack of time and resources for practice-based health promotion activities, and reluctance to refer patients may be barriers to the provision of more PC. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
