TY  - JOUR
T1  - Research in general practice for smokers and excessive drinkers in Australia and the UK: III. Dissemination of interventions
AN  - 618500174; 1994-34930-001
AB  - Discusses modes of delivery of interventions, including the mail, face-to-face strategies, training workshops, reinforcement contact after training, and teaching in medical school. Delivery of interventions by general practitioners (GPs) working in association with others such as the health visitor, health facilitator, practice nurse, and specialist clinic are examined. It is asserted that GPs underutilize their opportunities to identify and intervene with smokers and excessive drinkers. Barriers to intervention are explored, and potential new initiatives in general practice are identified, including matching GPs to specific treatments, comparing the uptake and continued use of different levels of interventions, evaluating the most effective ways of delivering interventions to GPs, and the training of doctors in intervention methods. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
