TY  - JOUR
T1  - Alcohol-related problems within the family and global functioning of the children: A population-based study
AN  - 618460996; 1994-21781-001
AB  - Conducted a population-based prevalence study to assess the association between the presence of alcohol-related problems within the family and the risk of disorders in children's global functioning level. 394 children attending nursery, primary, and secondary schools and their parents living in 2 municipalities in Central Italy served as Ss. Alcohol-related problems within the family were reported by registered records obtained from GPs and teachers. The children's level of functioning was assessed by teachers. A strong association was found between a poor level of functioning by children in the social environment and alcohol-related problems within the family, suggesting that the level of functioning of the child decreased as reports of alcohol-related problems in the family increased. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
