TY  - JOUR
T1  - Management of alcohol problems: The role of the general practitioner
AN  - 618418918; 1994-02108-001
AB  - Considers the role of the general practitioner (GP) in promoting behavioral change of the at-risk drinker, focusing on early intervention and the identification of such persons using screening or case-finding programs. The continuum of alcohol consumption and alcohol problems, the continuum of response to alcohol problems, brief interventions, the potential of primary health care, barriers to primary health care implementation, and effective treatment program management are considered. Evidence indicates early interventions by GPs are effective in reducing alcohol consumption among at-risk patients. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
