TY  - JOUR
T1  - Smoking habits in early pregnancy and attitudes towards smoking cessation among pregnant women and their partners
AN  - 618299140; 1993-27137-001
AB  - 187 GPs recorded smoking habits among 2,379 women, consulting for their 1st regular medical checkup in pregnancy. 46% of the women had been daily smokers the last 3 mo before pregnancy. 39% of Ss were still smoking at the time of their 1st checkup. 16% of the daily smokers stopped smoking spontaneously during the 1st few weeks of pregnancy. 57% of Ss younger than 20 and 28% of Ss aged 30 yrs and older did smoke at the 1st checkup. Single Ss smoked more often than Ss living with a partner. At the 1st checkup, 530 pregnant women, still smoking daily, and living with a partner, agreed to participate in a smoking intervention study. 65% reported a reduction in their use of cigarettes after becoming pregnant. Most Ss expressed motivation to quit or reduce their smoking habits during their pregnancy. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
