TY  - JOUR
T1  - Temazepam misuse in a group of injecting drug users
AN  - 618266993; 1993-13974-001
AB  - Studied the effects and complications of temazepam in its various formulations and explored reasons for its popularity among injecting drug users. Data from 23 temazepam injectors (aged 19–26 yrs) show that the group still found the gel-filled preparation readily injectable. This preparation appears to be more problematic in causing medical complications, including superficial thrombophlebitis, abscesses, and deep venous thrombosis. Various mental and psychological problems were also reported. Temazepam misuse can cause drug users to become more chaotic. GPs, who are the main source of temazepam prescribing, require additional training in prescribing to drug users. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
