T1  - A survey of general practitioners' opinion and attitude to drug addicts and addiction
AN  - 617760466; 1990-20008-001
AB  - Surveyed 203 general practitioners' (GPs) attitudes toward drug addicts and addiction. A range of negative and positive attitudes was identified. Male GPs, GPs in smaller practices, and those with addicts on their lists had a significantly more positive attitude toward drug addicts and their treatment. Government policy to encourage GPs to take a more active role in the management of drug addiction is likely to face difficulties. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
