TY  - JOUR
T1  - Heroin misusers: What they think of their general practitioners
AN  - 617755360; 1990-20888-001
AB  - Assessed 116 heroin misusers at hospital clinics regarding their contact with general practitioners (GPs), their routes of referral, and their estimation of GP reaction to a consultation regarding heroin misuse. 39 Ss had not previously contacted their GPs for drug misuse; 103 approached the specialized clinics through means other than a GP. The reported, or anticipated, responses concerning GP attitudes were generally unfavorable. Lack of training and support for GPs was a remediable explanation for the findings. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2022 APA, all rights reserved)
