TY  - JOUR
T1  - Shadowland: General practitioners and the treatment of opiate-abusing patients
AN  - 617544137; 1989-09888-001
AB  - Explored the experience of 23 general practitioners (GPs) currently being consulted by opiate-abusing patients. A combination of enhanced records and semi-structured interviews was used to collect detailed information on 50 consultations with opiate abusers. It was found that the GPs experienced much difficulty in sustaining a therapeutic role for themselves in relation to these patients. Certain themes cited repeatedly by the GPs stated that opiate-abusing patients were manipulative, adept liars, poorly motivated, and often aggressive. Strategies for dealing with such patients are presented. It is suggested that policymakers must clarify whether they want GPs to treat opiate abusers simply for the sake of treatment or in order to monitor a population at risk for human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
