T1  - The minister as a mental health worker
AN  - 615536564; 1968-10936-001
AB  - ALTHOUGH THE GREATEST CONCERN ABOUT RELIGION AND PSYCHIATRY RELATIONSHIPS HAS BEEN FOUND TO OCCUR IN INDUSTRIAL AND URBAN AREAS, IN THIS STUDY OF 9 CLERGYMEN "THERE WAS A HIGH WORKING CLASS OR RURAL PARISH REPRESENTATION." SIMILARITIES BETWEEN CLERGYMEN AND GENERAL PRACTIONERS (GPS) ARE NOTED, BUT SS LACKED THE SELF-CONFIDENCE OF GPS. PARISHONERS WHO SAW THE CLERGYMEN RATHER THAN A MENTAL HEALTH SPECIALIST INCLUDED SCHIZOPHRENICS, ALCOHOLICS, AND PEOPLE WITH MARITAL PROBLEMS AND MASKED DEPRESSIONS. IT IS URGED THAT THE CLERGYMEN NOT BE EXCLUDED FROM MENTAL HEALTH WORK WITH HIS PARISHONERS BY THE MEDICAL PROFESSION. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2017 APA, all rights reserved)
